// A minimal kicker carrier that is a PERMANENT ([CR#702.33a]) whose linked
// "if it was kicked" read happens in an enters-the-battlefield trigger, i.e.
// AFTER the spell has left the stack. [CR#702.33e] makes that read a linked
// ability ([CR#607]), and [CR#400.7d] is what lets it answer: "an ability of a
// permanent can reference information about the spell that became that
// permanent as it resolved, including what costs were paid to cast that
// spell". The record therefore has to survive the one stack -> battlefield
// zone change; the stack entry does not. Kicked -> 4 life, unkicked -> 2.
Normal(
    name: "Kicked Beast",
    mana_cost: [Green],
    types: [Creature],
    power: 2,
    toughness: 2,
    abilities: [
        Keyword(Kicker([Mana([Generic(2)])])),
        Triggered(
            event: ThisEnters,
            effect: If(
                condition: PaidCost(Kicker),
                then: ChangeLife(You, Up(4)),
                otherwise: ChangeLife(You, Up(2)),
            ),
        ),
    ],
)
